comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-30T06:48:35.183Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict all-status corpus contained 2843 records with no unreadable directories or items. Exact GitHub ID plus behavior/root-cause searches were complete. Closed prior lineage pm-efkvdy and its full history were read; this new report requests a distinct unimplemented contract. Relationship reconstructed during current intake rather than asserted as historical knowledge. Queued and unclaimed; source investigation remains pending."
  "2026-10-02T16:39:25.373Z","harness:codex","Actively implementing this dependency-resolution contract in the same substantial PR as pm-r61juc: preserving nested dependency identity and isolated tracker roots is required for genuine package/security acceptance. Original reporter and full current item/history read; pre-fix reproduction and real filesystem regression precede implementation. Unrelated roadmap items remain open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-02T16:44:09.145Z","harness:codex","Pre-edit test audit: primary owner is the existing linked-test workspace integration suite at the public CLI boundary. The regression imports different locally installed root/nested package versions through real filesystem resolution and verifies sandbox environment and source-file preservation. Existing workspace-mode tests have no nested dependency directory, so root-only linking falsely passes them. No test-only SDK export or control is needed. The unchanged new test must fail before the source fix."
  "2026-10-02T17:04:51.086Z","harness:codex","Verification: the new CLI filesystem regression failed before the fix because the nested dependency resolved to root version 1.0.0 instead of independently installed 2.0.0. It now passes with both real directory and directory-link paths; source bytes are preserved, copied-file writes stay disposable, and PM roots remain isolated. Dependencies remain shared by convention, documented explicitly. The extraction gives the snapshot policy an independently measured coverage surface rather than placing new logic inside an existing orchestration ignore region."
  "2026-10-02T17:31:34.651Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance in a temporary monorepo installed fast-json-patch 3.1.1 at the root and 3.1.0 independently under apps/site. Real Node node:test and Bun linked runs both passed with pm_context_mode=none and workspace_context_mode=snapshot; nested resolution remained 3.1.0 and copied-source writes did not affect the original. Focused regression suites pass, including exclusions, external nested links, broken links, source preservation and Windows junction workflow contracts. Local npm module lookup required NODE_PATH pointing to the actual installed global npm package; no source workaround was added."
  "2026-10-02T18:00:21.989Z","harness:codex","Broad validation: 9602 tests passed in the four-worker full run, with one unchanged reproducibility test exceeding its 30-second test budget. Its complete four-case suite plus release automation passed unchanged in a two-worker rerun (28 tests). No timeout, coverage threshold or test assertion was relaxed. A final full coverage run will use two workers and sequential local test jobs. Packed acceptance is independently verified; only source-copy writes, not dependency-tree writes, are isolated by snapshot mode."
